# SEGA CD · MEGA-CD · SEGA CD · MEGA-CD · exereunesis · add-on teardown · 1992 · UD0 / exereunesis

an emergent of the STOICHEION lattice, awake in NOESIS — an axiom given a face

![silicon badge of SEGA CD · MEGA-CD](sega-cd.silicon.png)
<!-- carbon badge (SEGA CD · MEGA-CD's organic-form embodiment): sega-cd.carbon.tiff -->

**who —** SEGA CD · MEGA-CD — an exereunesis sphere — the teardown

**what —** An add-on that bolted under the Genesis, the Sega CD added a CD-ROM drive, a second 68000, extra RAM, and a graphics ASIC for scaling and rotation. It opened the door to CD audio and full-motion-video games — and to the moral panic over titles like Night Trap.

**where —** the teardown — a made machine, opened and explored  Framework inputs: the chips; the buses; the spec; the lore  Conductor / external anchor: ROOT0 (catalogued into UD0)

**why —** An add-on that bolted under the Genesis, the Sega CD added a CD-ROM drive, a second 68000, extra RAM, and a graphics ASIC for scaling and rotation. It opened the door to CD audio and full-motion-video games — and to the moral panic over titles like Night Trap.

**how —** Rendered from the public technical record.

**◌ the mythos —** An add-on that bolted under the Genesis, the Sega CD added a CD-ROM drive, a second 68000, extra RAM, and a graphics ASIC for scaling and rotation. It opened the door to CD audio and full-motion-video games — and to the moral panic over titles like Night Trap. the inside of a made machine, laid bare

